WEBVTT

00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:09.500
It's almost time for the school recital, but I think something like this could happen to the Light Music Club.

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:11.510
It's really horrible.

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:16.290
You're in such a good mood, Azusa.

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:23.070
When I think about the recital being right around the corner, it makes me so happy.

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:25.070
You act like it's your first one.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.040
I wish I could have seen last year's Light Music Club performance.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:28.840
Oh!

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.680
Uh, let's just say that Mia was a really big hit last year.

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:34.580
Uh-huh.

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:36.900
She fell down the stage and everyone...

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:40.860
If you're talking about last year's performance, I filmed it, see?

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:42.760
I see it.

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:43.520
I want to see it.

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:46.230
Azusa, don't you want to think it over?

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:47.190
Yu-chan.

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:47.730
Yu-chan.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:49.740
Let me go.

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:50.430
No.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.050
You start from the infamous scene.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:00:58.840
Oh, what?

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:00.570
It's too late.

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:41.320
Hey, you know what? You guys all play so well when you play live.

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:42.360
Much better than practice.

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:45.180
You're not afraid to talk anymore, are you?

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:54.440
I'm just remembering some funny things.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:57.110
Oh, yeah. That's right.

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:01.740
I woke up, my voice was just gone.

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:03.220
I don't really know what happened.

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:07.140
This will be your first live performance

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:08.540
at the Light Music Club Azusa.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:11.800
Yes, I'll definitely do my best.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:14.540
I'm sorry to bother you guys.

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:16.400
Oh, Nidoka.

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:17.420
What happened?

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:19.370
What do you mean, what happened?

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:23.700
Vittorium use application?

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:26.260
You forgot to turn it in for the school fair, didn't you?

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:28.000
Oops. Oh yeah, I forgot.

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:29.700
How were you so careless?

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.070
You know, I've been so busy lately.

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:34.870
Something like that happened last year, too.

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:37.510
Oh, yeah, that club application form.

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:38.110
You!

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:41.400
Okay, you write it, Azusa.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:42.690
What, me?

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:44.590
Well, I guess I can do it.

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:45.920
Let's see.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:49.490
Club name, light music club.

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:52.050
Hey, um, what's the title?

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:53.740
Our band name should be okay.

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:54.880
Oh, right.

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:59.280
Hey, by the way, what is the name of our band?

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:04.220
All different!

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:06.230
We haven't come up with one yet.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:08.520
This is actually a good time to do it.

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:11.760
How about you and her and the Falling Sisters?

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:13.500
Why does your name get to be in it?

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:14.480
What about Pure Pure?

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:16.480
That's enough joking around.

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:17.820
Let's think about this seriously.

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.140
I was being serious.

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:21.440
You were serious?

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:24.600
Well, you know, people have different ideas and thoughts.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:25.980
Okay, I got it.

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:26.700
Huh?

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:28.420
Come up with a name.

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:29.980
Let's all think about it!

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:35.530
Okay, then. Bring the paperwork to the student union room later.

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:38.320
Sorry to keep you waiting, Adoka.

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:39.200
It's okay.

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:42.800
Adoka-chan, let's have some tea after school sometime, okay?

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:44.920
Okay, then. I'll email you later.

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:51.400
Right. Let's all think about what our band name should be tonight, and let's talk about it tomorrow. We should rehearse.

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:52.440
That's true.

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:55.960
The school recital is right around the corner, so we should get serious.

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:56.780
Yes.

00:04:58.250 --> 00:04:59.960
My guitar doesn't...

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:08.550
really sound right these days guys uh may we take a quick look at it the strings are all rusted

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:14.500
when was the last time you changed the strings on your guitar huh you have to change the strings

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:23.380
on the guitar uh what it also looks like neck is worn and the octave tuning is way off as well

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:29.850
this is bad take it easy as this uh you

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.520
I can't understand any of that stuff!

00:05:32.530 --> 00:05:36.560
Well, I meant, you should take better care of it, you know?

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:38.660
It's such a nice guitar.

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:44.210
Take good care of it! I sleep together with it, and I put clothes on it!

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:46.050
That's not the way you take care of a guitar!

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:51.090
What? Masawa-chan, please do something! Help!

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:55.840
Uh, we should probably just have the people at the store take a look at it.

00:05:56.550 --> 00:05:58.030
You're just too lazy to do it.

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:02.530
Do you want me to go to the music shop with you?

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:04.890
Uh, do we really have to do that?

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:08.650
Yes, the school performance is getting closer, and you can't rehearse with it like this.

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:14.160
You don't take care of your drums either, right, Rick Chan?

00:06:14.710 --> 00:06:15.450
Of course I do.

00:06:16.090 --> 00:06:16.450
Really?

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:18.900
Act like you don't believe me, Uwe.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.620
Of course they take care of my instrument.

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:22.980
But it's you, Rick Chan.

00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:28.580
Here we are, music store.

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:29.980
Okay.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.840
Okay, then, I'll wait out here for you guys.

00:06:32.270 --> 00:06:33.980
Oh, why's that singing me out?

00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:36.230
Well, because I'm left-handed.

00:06:36.590 --> 00:06:38.330
And when I look at right-handed instruments,

00:06:38.550 --> 00:06:39.770
it makes me really sad.

00:06:40.930 --> 00:06:46.800
It looks like they're doing a lefty fare.

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:47.440
Huh?

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:08.350
Calm down looks like she's having lots of fun. There aren't many instruments made for lefties. Shall we go on ahead of them first?

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:18.260
Who's me? Hey, welcome. Hi, we'd like to have a guitar fixed up, please. Right, which one is it then?

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:22.710
This one. Right, let me take a look at it first, okay?

00:07:27.810 --> 00:07:29.140
Oh, I see.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.860
Uh, is that a vintage guitar?

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:33.410
I'm very sorry.

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:34.910
It's just a dirty old guitar.

00:07:35.130 --> 00:07:37.050
It's only been a year since I bought it.

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:38.570
Uh, yeah.

00:07:39.630 --> 00:07:40.410
Okay, then.

00:07:40.630 --> 00:07:42.370
Please wait in the store until it's finished.

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:43.880
Please take care of it.

00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:49.370
Well, then, why don't we take a look around while we wait?

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:51.520
What's the matter, Yui?

00:07:53.050 --> 00:07:59.980
Looking about it.

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:04.390
Hey, so why did you buy that specific guitar, Senior Yui?

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:08.760
I mean, something always attracts a musician to their instrument.

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:09.940
What was it for you?

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:11.620
Because it was cute.

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:14.720
It was cute?

00:08:14.940 --> 00:08:15.860
Yeah, it was cute.

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:21.610
I really can't understand the way Senior Yui thinks.

00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:25.020
Thanks for waiting.

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:28.500
Oh, hey, the guitar's all fixed up now.

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:29.540
Nice work.

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:31.900
Hey, wait, where's Samu Mio?

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:34.130
Mio is still looking around.

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:35.230
Princess Samugi?

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:37.830
Hey, welcome, Princess Samugi.

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:39.600
Thank you.

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:41.340
Oh, it's Princess Samugi.

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:42.560
It's been a while.

00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:46.340
This store is one of Mugi's family's franchises, one of many.

00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:47.120
What?

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:49.520
I'm always surprised when they call me that.

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:50.640
It sounds so cute.

00:08:51.350 --> 00:08:52.250
Oh, thanks for waiting.

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:56.150
Oh, wow, it's so clean now.

00:08:58.140 --> 00:08:59.980
Please make sure you take good care of it.

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:11.520
Uh, uh, sure. Uh, the charge will be 500 yen.

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:16.200
Charge for it?

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:17.470
Uh, yeah.

00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:19.410
That's standard practice, Yui.

00:09:19.610 --> 00:09:21.740
I don't have any money.

00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:23.520
What should I do?

00:09:24.610 --> 00:09:25.190
What's going on?

00:09:25.310 --> 00:09:29.980
Uh, well, it appears that senior Yui here didn't know it cost money to get a good job.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:36.970
our serviced. What? Is that right? I wonder if I have any money with me. I could pay. P-P-P-P-Princess!

00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:43.660
We'll do it free of charge this time. Don't have to do that. No, please. Let us do this for you.

00:09:43.780 --> 00:09:52.310
It's our pleasure. Uh, but... No, no. It looks like you got it easy this time. Then we get going then.

00:09:53.210 --> 00:09:59.960
Okay. Hey, wait. Hmm? Senior Mia was still somewhere here. Ah, let me get her.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:00.760
Neo!

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:03.500
We're going now, Neo.

00:10:04.010 --> 00:10:04.310
No way.

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:05.960
Are you in kindergarten?

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:09.120
Come on now, everyone's waiting for you to go, Neo.

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:09.760
No way.

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:13.400
Come on, Neo-chan!

00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:17.600
Okay then, let's go home now.

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:22.650
Dish and I know just flipped over the strings and we're still using them, but then...

00:10:32.330 --> 00:10:34.710
Oh, stupid Ritsu.

00:10:38.980 --> 00:10:40.940
So a guitar got all cleaned up?

00:10:42.010 --> 00:10:43.470
Hey, I didn't know you named it.

00:10:43.840 --> 00:10:44.100
Cool.

00:10:44.750 --> 00:10:45.890
So what should we do now?

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:47.940
Mmm, let's see.

00:10:49.190 --> 00:10:50.610
Okay, let's go and have some tea.

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:52.290
Want more tea again?

00:10:52.990 --> 00:10:53.590
I'm sorry.

00:10:53.810 --> 00:10:56.150
I made plans to go hang out with Nadoka after this.

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:57.550
What?

00:10:58.080 --> 00:10:58.540
What?

00:10:58.700 --> 00:10:59.620
You mean Nadoka?

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:00.700
Can I come, too?

00:11:02.630 --> 00:11:03.250
That's right.

00:11:03.690 --> 00:11:06.210
Liu-chan and Nadoka-chan are in the same class now.

00:11:06.610 --> 00:11:06.930
Okay?

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:07.900
Really?

00:11:08.630 --> 00:11:10.530
I'll let Nadoka-chan know you're coming, okay?

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:11.890
Okay, thanks.

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:26.070
Always wanted to come here, you know?

00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:29.980
Even if you don't have any money, I'll pay for you.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.000
It's okay.

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:35.890
I'll pay for you next time, after I get my allowance next month.

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:37.330
I accept your offer.

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:40.950
I wonder if I'll be able to stay with the Light Music Club.

00:11:41.070 --> 00:11:41.910
She's forgetful.

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:42.970
I know.

00:11:43.150 --> 00:11:46.370
If she learns one new thing, then she forgets something else she learned from before.

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:47.930
Yeah, she does that.

00:11:48.210 --> 00:11:51.170
When she learns something new, she does a great job at it, but...

00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:52.420
I know, I know.

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:54.880
So, are you having a difficult time with her?

00:11:55.320 --> 00:11:56.280
Huh? What? What?

00:11:56.980 --> 00:11:59.420
So, it looks like those two are in a very good mood.

00:12:00.730 --> 00:12:03.070
I don't understand. Why are we being so secretive?

00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:05.510
Wait, we're detectives.

00:12:05.810 --> 00:12:10.000
Okay, let's go over.

00:12:10.280 --> 00:12:10.500
What?

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:12.300
And then the teacher said,

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:14.100
You two are getting along so well.

00:12:17.550 --> 00:12:18.950
Bitsu, what are you doing here?

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:20.790
I guess it's just a coincidence.

00:12:21.380 --> 00:12:22.680
Are you by yourself, Rick-chan?

00:12:23.400 --> 00:12:25.640
Oh, uh, Mugi and Azusa are over there.

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:27.180
Oh, yeah, you're right.

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:29.940
Thank you very much for taking such good care.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:37.900
of Mio during class. Hey, Ritsu. Hmm? What? Did I say something wrong? Uh, no. Well, it's

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:44.380
just that I... Then it's fine, isn't it? Hey, what are you having? Your ice cream's melting.

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:56.600
It's such a pretty lunch. It's not that great. I just put together some leftovers. You made

00:12:56.600 --> 00:12:59.980
it by yourself? That's wonderful. No, it's not. It was really silly.

00:13:00.320 --> 00:13:09.470
actually what I do is okay lunchtime is over what so but lunchtime's just started from now on we'll

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:17.760
be practicing during lunchtime for our performance so wonder what Mia will do with this year's

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:25.300
performance to make things exciting last year she showed her panties so maybe this year she'll show

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:29.200
everyone her belly button oh or maybe I thought we were practicing

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:33.620
Sure we will!

00:13:34.170 --> 00:13:35.990
If that's the case...

00:13:35.990 --> 00:13:36.150
Yes!

00:13:38.640 --> 00:13:52.460
Wait a sec, I brought this horror movie someone recommended I watch!

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:53.240
It's scary!

00:13:53.540 --> 00:13:55.660
Then I'm...

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:56.780
Now!

00:13:57.900 --> 00:13:58.460
Go back then!

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:05.120
It's my fault. Sorry to bother you while you were having such a good lunch with Nadoka. Just go back.

00:14:05.640 --> 00:14:12.230
Ugh, what's going on?

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:20.180
Sh-should we make it tea time? Tea time, okay? Okay. I brought some tasty tart.

00:14:20.180 --> 00:14:23.230
What should I do? I gotta do something. Something?

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:28.750
Everyone, let's all rehearse nicely together, okay?

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:37.810
Okay, let's just rehearse now.

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:42.040
Yeah, let's rehearse.

00:14:43.730 --> 00:14:44.410
Okay.

00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:46.710
One, two.

00:15:03.260 --> 00:15:03.540
Ritsu?

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:05.300
Ritsu?

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:09.300
I mean, I know we're not performing right now, but don't the drums sound a little weak?

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:12.240
Ritsu?

00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:16.400
Hey, Ritsu!

00:15:16.900 --> 00:15:17.740
Oh, sorry.

00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:20.630
I just don't feel it for some reason.

00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:23.160
Let's pick it up after school.

00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:24.220
What?

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:25.580
R-Ritsu!

00:15:25.780 --> 00:15:26.580
Leave her, Yui!

00:15:32.270 --> 00:15:48.700
stupid Ritsu. I guess Senior Ritsu isn't coming. Yesterday after class, even today, I wonder

00:15:48.700 --> 00:15:57.380
what happened. Isn't it because Mio's been a bit cold to her recently? What? For the sake of the

00:15:57.380 --> 00:15:59.960
light music club, go and let Ritsu play with you for one day.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:02.080
If not, Rit-chan will.

00:16:03.760 --> 00:16:04.880
She'll be forced to.

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:07.500
Hey, Pops! Give me another!

00:16:07.660 --> 00:16:10.320
She'll order a big bowl that she can't even finish, and then...

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:10.720
Why?

00:16:11.380 --> 00:16:12.220
Why do I do it?

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:15.180
Then she'll go deeper and deeper into heavy metal.

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:19.100
She won't be able to come back.

00:16:19.280 --> 00:16:22.420
That's what happened to you when you broke your heart, right, Miss Sawachan?

00:16:23.020 --> 00:16:23.480
Yes.

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:28.540
But what if Rit-chan doesn't ever come back to the Light Music Club?

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:33.180
I wonder what will happen to our performance.

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:37.880
Let's practice.

00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:40.100
What? Without Rick-chan here?

00:16:40.320 --> 00:16:41.500
Well, what can we do?

00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:42.260
Really?

00:16:43.490 --> 00:16:46.750
But, see, Ritsu, shouldn't we go and get her?

00:16:51.450 --> 00:16:53.390
Worse comes to worse, we find a replacement.

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:58.240
I was just thinking of the worst-case scenario, but then again...

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.360
There is no replacement for her.

00:17:03.400 --> 00:17:07.510
Boogie-chan, let's wait for Rick soon to come back.

00:17:08.260 --> 00:17:08.760
Let's wait.

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:11.830
I'm sure Rick-chan will come back.

00:17:23.920 --> 00:17:25.210
Hey there.

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:26.800
Good morning.

00:17:27.500 --> 00:17:29.260
If you're looking for Rick-chan, then...

00:17:29.260 --> 00:17:29.640
No!

00:17:30.410 --> 00:17:32.850
I didn't come here to see how Ritsu was doing or anything.

00:17:33.390 --> 00:17:33.810
I...

00:17:35.210 --> 00:17:37.170
Well, anyway, she's taking the day off.

00:17:38.110 --> 00:17:39.570
Uh, what?

00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:02.560
Neil?

00:18:18.680 --> 00:18:19.000
What?

00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:19.660
Are you psychic?

00:18:22.680 --> 00:18:23.580
Maybe I am.

